		<Placemark>
			<name>B-1B Lancer</name>
			<description><![CDATA[Guam is used as a stage for ferrying aircraft. There is a report from May 9, 2006 about a B-1 having to make a wheels-up landing at Diego Garcia. It was the end of a ferry mission from Texas, which included a stop at Guam apparently. That's not THIS aircraft, but it demonstates the path they use. In 2003 the US Government stationed B1 and B52 bombers at Guam to 'make a point' to North Korea, but as there are no active B-52 bombers visible, I suspect those have all returned to their original bases by the time this image was taken in 2005.<p>

http://www.fas.org/nuke/guide/usa/bomber/b-1b_gallery.htm<br>
<center><img width=300 src="http://www.fas.org/nuke/guide/usa/bomber/b-1b-0702b1b.jpg"></center>]]></description>
			<LookAt>
				<longitude>144.9236830135058</longitude>
				<latitude>13.57508985499345</latitude>
				<altitude>0</altitude>
				<range>195.9224506856731</range>
				<tilt>1.167759142479322e-009</tilt>
				<heading>0.04518258861363409</heading>
			</LookAt>
			<styleUrl>C:\WINNT\Temp\Temporary Internet Files\Content.IE5\0DK345UJ\441516-GuamAircraft[1].kmz#khStyle640_copy0</styleUrl>
			<Point>
				<coordinates>144.9235784184899,13.57538962019938,0</coordinates>
			</Point>
		</Placemark>
		<Placemark>
			<name>3 B-1B Lancers</name>
			<description><![CDATA[Guam is used as a stage for ferrying aircraft. There is a report from May 9, 2006 about a B-1 having to make a wheels-up landing at Diego Garcia. It was the end of a ferry mission from Texas, which included a stop at Guam apparently. That's not THIS aircraft, but it demonstates the path they use. In 2003 the US Government stationed B1 and B52 bombers at Guam to 'make a point' to North Korea, but as there are no active B-52 bombers visible, I suspect those have all returned to their original bases by the time this image was taken in 2005.<p>

http://www.fas.org/nuke/guide/usa/bomber/b-1b_gallery.htm<br>
<center><img width=300 src="http://www.fas.org/nuke/guide/usa/bomber/b-1b-0702b1b.jpg"></center>]]></description>
			<LookAt>
				<longitude>144.9207371202207</longitude>
				<latitude>13.57423008928378</latitude>
				<altitude>0</altitude>
				<range>576.9692012499186</range>
				<tilt>6.077319032477457e-011</tilt>
				<heading>-0.001002352259207049</heading>
			</LookAt>
			<styleUrl>C:\WINNT\Temp\Temporary Internet Files\Content.IE5\0DK345UJ\441516-GuamAircraft[1].kmz#khStyle640_copy0</styleUrl>
			<Point>
				<coordinates>144.9211287671336,13.57450782766756,0</coordinates>
			</Point>
		</Placemark>
		<Placemark>
			<name>B-52 display</name>
			<description><![CDATA[This isn't a flyable aircraft.<p>

Here's a link to some B-52 memorial images. The Guam memorial is down the page a short ways.<br>
http://www.306thbw.org/306thscrpbk/scpbkMmrls.htm<p>
<center><img width=300 src="http://www.306thbw.org/306thscrpbk/images/GUAMMEMORIALB52.JPG"></center>]]></description>
			<LookAt>
